# MIS Report → CO Performance — Frontend API & UI Guide

Menu: **MIS Report → CO Performance**

Compares the field officers (**CO / Sahayika**) for a period (**From date – To date**): outreach, disbursement, portfolio, collection efficiency and portfolio at risk (PAR). Each Sahayika gets a grade and a rank. Drill down to the groups of a Sahayika, and see a month-wise trend. Read-only screen.

| Purpose | Method | URL |
|---|---|---|
| Branch dropdown (head office only) | GET | `/api/Org/ProcessMaster/GetBranchList` (existing) |
| Sahayika dropdown (optional filter) | GET | `/api/Org/ProcessLoan/GetSahayikaList` (existing) |
| **CO Performance** | GET | `/api/Org/MisReport/CoPerformance` |

Needs the Sanctum token (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`) and `Accept: application/json` / `Content-Type: application/json`, the same as other APIs.

---

## How the figures are calculated

A loan belongs to the Sahayika of the **loan**, else of its **group**, else of the **member**; otherwise it is **Not Assigned** (same rule as Demand Generation and Demand vs Collection). Demand / collection / overdue figures are exactly the same as in the *Demand vs Collection* report for the same filters.

| Block | Field | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Outreach | `Active_Loan_Count` | Loans with outstanding > 0 at *To* |
| | `Active_Member_Count`, `Active_Group_Count` | Borrowers / groups having an active loan |
| | `New_Group_Count` | Groups admitted (`Adm_Date`) in the period |
| | `New_Member_Count` | Members admitted (`Admission_Date`) in the period |
| Disbursement | `Disb_Count`, `Disb_Amount` | Loans disbursed in the period (loan amount) |
| | `Avg_Loan_Size` | `Disb_Amount ÷ Disb_Count` (`null` when no disbursement) |
| Portfolio | `Opening_Outstanding` | Loan balance before *From* (realisable − collected) |
| | `Outstanding` | Loan balance at *To* |
| | `Closed_Loan_Count` | Loans fully repaid during the period |
| Collection | `Arrear_Demand`, `Current_Demand` | Overdue at *From*; installments due in the period |
| | `Net_Demand` | Arrear + Current − advance already paid |
| | `Coll_Against_Demand` | Collection that cleared demand (arrear + current) |
| | `Coll_Advance` | Collected beyond the demand |
| | `Coll_Amount` | Total collected in the period |
| | `Coll_Pct` | `Coll_Against_Demand ÷ Net_Demand × 100` (`null` when no demand) |
| | `Overdue_Amount`, `Overdue_Account_Count` | Unpaid demand at *To* and number of such loans |
| Risk | `PAR_Amount` | **Outstanding** of all loans that have any overdue at *To* |
| | `PAR_Pct` | `PAR_Amount ÷ Outstanding × 100` |
| | `PAR_0_30`, `PAR_31_60`, `PAR_61_90`, `PAR_Above_90` | `PAR_Amount` split by days since the oldest unpaid installment |
| Rating | `Grade` | By `Coll_Pct`: **A** ≥ 95, **B** ≥ 85, **C** ≥ 70, **D** < 70. `null` when no demand |
| | `Perf_Rank` | 1 = best. Rank by `Coll_Pct` (high first), then `PAR_Pct` (low first). `null` when no demand |

Every Sahayika of the branch is listed, even with no activity (all zeros, no grade / rank). Loans without a Sahayika appear as a **Not Assigned** row (`Key_Id = 0`) per branch.

**Branch rule**
- Head office user: All Branches or any single branch via `report_branch_id`.
- Branch user: always their own branch; `report_branch_id` is ignored.

